{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2025-57803",
    "CVE-2025-55298"
  ],
  "description": "Woojin Park, Hojun Lee, Yougin Won and Siyeon Han discovered that\nImageMagick did not properly sanitize image file names. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause a denial of service, obtain sensitive\ninformation, or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2025-55298)\n\nLumina Mescuwa discovered that ImageMagick did not properly handle memory\nwhen encoding BMP images. An attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause ImageMagick to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly\nexecute arbitrary code. (CVE-2025-57803)",
  "id": "USN-7812-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in ImageMagick.",
